$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Mitsunobu Reaction of amino alcohols with nitrophenols:
(1S,2R)-N,N-dimethylephedrine (1.0 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (0.1M)
with the nitrophenol (1.5 equiv.) and triphenylphosphine (1.5 equiv.).
Diisopropylazodicarboxylate (1.5 equiv.) was then added by syringe and
the reaction mixture stirred for 12h, then diluted with EtOAc and washed
with 1M NaOH (x 2) and brine (x 1). The EtOAc layer was then dried over
K2CO3 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue thus obtained
was chromatographed over SiO2 to yield the aminoether.
(1R,2S)-Dimethyl-[1-methyl-2-(2-nitrophenoxy)-2-phenylethyl]-amine.
Yield: 83% (Mitsunobu), 98% (SNAr). Rf = 0.37 (TEA-washed SiO2,
Hexanes/EtOAc/TEA : 50:50:1). Rf = 0.37 IR (film/cm-1): 2937m, 2825m,
2781m, 1605s, 1525s, 1485s, 1452s, 1353s, 1277s, 1253s, 991s, 860s, 743s,
701s. δH (500MHz, CDCl3): 1.18 (d, J7Hz, 3H, -CHCH3), 2.36 (s, 6H,
-NCH3), 2.96 (dq, J7Hz, 3Hz, 1H, -NCHCH3), 5.51 (d, J3Hz, 1H, -OCHPh),
6.79 (d, J9Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 6.92 (t, J8Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.25-7.35 (m, 6H,
Ar-H), 7.82 (m, 1H, Ar-H).δc (125MHz, CDCl3): 7.8 (-CHCH3), 41.7 (-NCH3),
65.6 (-NCHCH3), 81.5 (-OCHPh), 115.6, 120.1, 125.6, 126.0, 127.8, 128.7,
133.9, 139.2, 140.1, 150.8. m/z (ESI): 301 (MH+:100%). HRMS found
301.1547. C17H21N2O3 (MH+) requires 301.1552. [α]D (23°C) = -65.7 (c =
0.9, CHCl3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternate preparation described, Mitsunobu reaction
