$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the epoxide synthesis
(Scheme S-2) In a round-bottomed flask the desired diol and phosphine
were disolved in anhydrous CH2Cl2 at room temperature. Next, neat DIAD
was added dropwise (5-10 seconds) and the reaction progress was followed
by TLC. Once the reaction finished, the solvent was removed under vacuum
and the crude purified by column chromatography (on SiO2/NEt3 2.5%,
hexane as eluent). 2,2-bis(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-3-phenyloxirane
(2f) Prepared according to general procedure from a solution of
(S)-1,1-bis(4- trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-2-phenylethane-1,2-diol 1f (50 mg,
0.117 mmols, 1 eq), phosphine (0.123 mmols, 1.05 eq), anhydrous CH2Cl2
(0.5 mL) and DIAD (24 μL, 0.123 mmols, 1.05 eq). A white solid or
colorless oil is obtained (depending on which is the enantiomeric purity)
after purification. Yields and ee's, depending on the phosphine used, are
shown in the article. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.34 (s, 1H), 6.98-7.05
(m, 2H), 7.13-7.21 (m, 3H), 7.32 (d, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (dd, J = 11 Hz,
J = 8 Hz, 4H), 7.61 (d, J = 8 Hz, 2H) ppm; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-63.06 (s, 1F), -63.09 (s, 1F) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 67.8 (C),
68.3 (CH), 125.2 (q, JF = 4 Hz, CH), 125.7 (q, JF = 4 Hz, CH), 126.7
(CH), 126.7 (q, JF = 272 Hz, C), 126.8 (q, JF = 271, C), 126.8 (CH),
128.2 (CH), 128.4 (CH), 129.7 (CH), 130.5 (q, JF = 32 Hz, C), 130.6 (q,
JF = 32 Hz, C), 134.3 (C), 139.2 (C), 144.0 (C) ppm; IR (NaCl): νmax.
2924, 1619, 1324, 1127, 833 cm-1; MS (CI-NH3) m/z : 426.9 [M+NH4 +,
100%]; [α]D -65.3 (c 1.01, CHCl3) R enantiomer 99 % ee; Mp 90-93°C;
ANALYSIS Calct for C22H14F6O: C 64.71 H 3.46, Found C 64.33 H 3.37; HPLC
Daicel CHIRALCEL-ODR. MeOH/NaClO4-HClO4 pH=2 solution 95:5, 0.5 mL/min, λ
= 254 nm, tR (S) = 9.8 min, tR (R) = 13.1 min.
