$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 8. Mitsunobu Reaction: A glass vial,
screwcapped with a teflon-lined septum containing the polymer supported
aminoalcohol (70mg, 0.70 mmol/g) was charged with 2 mL of a stock
solution of tributylphosphine (3.1 mL, 12.6 mmol) and bromophenol (12.6
mmol) in THF (60 mL). The suspension was gently agitated for 10 min and
then cooled to -78°C. 1 mL of a stock solution of TMAD in THF (2.16 g,
12.6 mmol in 31 mL) was then added dropwise with constant agitation. The
reaction mixture was then allowed to slowly warm to room temperature and
agitated for 24 h at ambient temperature and the solution drained. The
beads were washed with 100:1 DMF/TEA (3 x 30 min), 50:50:1 THF/DMF/TEA (3
x 30 min), 100:1 THF/TEA (3 x 30 min), and CH2Cl2 (4 x 30 min); then
dried in vacuo ( house-vacuum for 2h, then high-vacuum for 12 h).
Cleavage of compound from resin was followed by purification and
spectroscopic characterization. 2. General procedure for Cleavage of
Compound from Resin: 5-40 mg of beads were transferred to a 1.7mL
microcentrifuge eppendorf or 20 mL polypropylene vial and freshly
prepared HF.Py/Py/THF (90:5:5 by volume, 100 μL per 10mg beads) was
added. The beads were gently agitated for 1.5 h and the excess HF
quenched by addition of methoxytrimethylsilane (100 μL per 10 mg beads)
and the beads further agitated for 1h. The beads were filtered and
further washed with freshly distilled THF (x 2) and MeCN (x 2). The
washings and filtrate were combined, filtered through a pad of SiO2 and
concentrated under reduced pressure to yield the library compound.
4-Bromo-3-({[2S-(2-bromopyridin-3-yloxy)-1R-methyl-2-phenylethyl]-methyl-amino}-methyl)-phenol,
A1B7D2. Colorless oil. Yield: 82%; Rf = 0.43 (SiO2, Ethyl Actetate). Rf =
0.43 δH (500MHz, CDCl3): 1.35 (d, J7Hz, 3H, NCHCH3), 2.39 (s, 3H, NCH3),
3.15 (dq, J7Hz, 5Hz, 1H, NCHCH3), 3.65 (d, J15Hz, 1H, ArCHH'N), 3.76 (d,
J15Hz, 1H, ArCHH'N), 5.31 (d, J5Hz, 1H, OCHPh), 6.49 (d, J3Hz, 1H, Ar-H),
6.57 (dd, J8.5Hz, 3Hz, 1H, Ar- H), 6.85 (dd, J8.5Hz, 1.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H),
6.98 (dd, J8Hz, 4.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H), 7.29 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 7.34 (d, J7Hz, 1H,
Ar-H), 7.87 (dd, J4.5Hz, 1.5Hz, 1H, Ar-H). δc (125MHz, CDCl3): 9.2, 37.9,
58.3, 64.0, 82.5, 113.8, 115.5, 117.0, 121.1, 123.2, 126.6, 127.7, 128.3,
128.7, 133.2, 139.2, 139.5, 141.0, 151.1, 155.2. m/z (ESI): 505 (MH+,
79Br, 79Br; 50%), 507 (MH+, 79Br, 81Br; 100%).HRMS found 505.0126.
C22H23Br2N2O2 (MH+, 79Br) requires 505.0122.
