$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the epoxide synthesis
(Scheme S-2) In a round-bottomed flask the desired diol and phosphine
were disolved in anhydrous CH2Cl2 at room temperature. Next, neat DIAD
was added dropwise (5-10 seconds) and the reaction progress was followed
by TLC. Once the reaction finished, the solvent was removed under vacuum
and the crude purified by column chromatography (on SiO2/NEt3 2.5%,
hexane as eluent). 2,2-bis(4-fluorophenyl)-3-phenyloxirane (2e) 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.28 (s, 1H), 6.89 (ddd, JF = 9 Hz, J = 3 Hz, J = 3
Hz, 1H), 6.91 (ddd, JF = 9 Hz, J = 3 Hz, J = 3 Hz, 1H), 6.98-7.06 (m,
4H), 7.12-7.20 (m, 5H), 7.27-7.33 (m, 2H) ppm; 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ
-114.03 (m, 1F), -114.66 (m, 1F) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 67.7
(C), 68.2 (CH), 115.1 (d, JF = 22 Hz, CH), 115.5 (d, JF = 21 Hz, CH),
126.8 (CH), 128.0 (CH), 128.0 (CH), 128.2 (d, JF = 8 Hz, CH), 130.9 (d,
JF = 8 Hz, CH), 131.7 (d, JF = 3 Hz, C), 135.1 (C), 136.7 (d, JF = 3 Hz,
C), 162.2 (d, JF = 245 Hz, C), 162.6 (d, JF = 246 Hz, C) ppm; IR (NaCl):
νmax. 3065, 1604, 1510, 1224, 834 cm-1; MS (CI-NH3) m/z : 325.9 [M+NH4 +,
100%], 308.8 [M+, 81%]; [α]D -61.7 (c 0.75, CHCl3) R enantiomer 99 % ee;
Mp 82-85°C; HRMS (ESI-TOF): Calct for C20H15F2O: 309.1091, Found
309.1085; HPLC Daicel CHIRALPAK-AD. Heptane/i-PrOH 90:10, 0.5 mL/min, λ =
254 nm, tR (S) = 7.3 min, tR (R) = 9.2 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu cyclodeyhydration
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Phosphine-Dependent Stereoselectivity in the Mitsunobu Cyclodehydration
of 1,2-Diols: Stereodivergent Approach to Triaryl-Substituted Epoxides
