$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Aryl Alkyl Ether Formation under Mitsunobu
Conditions; General Procedure (GP2) The secondary alcohol (1.0 equiv),
the phenol (1.2 equiv) and PPh3 (1.2 equiv) were dissolved in THF (c =
0.1-0.2 M). After addition of DEAD/DIAD (1.4 equiv) the reaction was
stirred until conversion was complete (40 °C, 3-6 h). Subsequently, the
solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was directly purified by
FCC. The intermediate was treated with TBAF·3H2O (17.9 g, 50.9 mmol) in
THF (150 mL). Stirring at r.t. for 15 min and standard work-up (sat.
NH4Cl, EtOAc) and FCC purification (PE-EtOAc, 1:2 → EtOAc) provided 29.
2-O-(3'
-Cyanophenyl)-5-O-[4''-(2'''-tert-butylamino-sulfonylphenyl)-phenyl]-1,4:3,6-dianhydro-D-sorbitole
(44); Typical Procedure. Compound 41 (206 mg, 475 mmol) was treated with
PPh3 (150 mg, 572 mmol), hydroxy-benzonitrile (93 mg, 781 mmol) and DEAD
(105 mL, 667 mmol) according to GP2. FCC purification (CH2Cl2- MeOH,
100:1 → 50:1) resulted in phenyl ether 44 (205 mg, 383 mmol, 81%) as a
colorless solid. mp 144 °C (MTBE); Rf = 0.15 (CH2Cl2-MeOH, 100:1); [α]589
= 63, [α]578 = 66, [α]546 = 75, [α]436 = 130 (c = 1.024, CHCl3, 22 °C).
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.99 (s, 9 H), 3.59 (br s, 1 H), 4.04-4.14
(m, 3 H), 4.25 (dd, J = 10.5, 4.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.65 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H),
4.84-4.89 (m, 2 H), 5.03 (t, J = 5.1 Hz, 1 H), 7.06 (pd, J = 8.8 Hz, 2
H), 7.14-7.22 (m, 2 H), 7.28-7.32 (m, 2 H), 7.41 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H),
7.43-7.49 (m, 3 H), 7.55 (td, J = 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 8.16 (dd, J = 7.9,
1.4 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 29.7, 54.4, 71.3, 73.2, 77.5,
81.4, 82.0, 86.0, 113.5, 114.8, 118.4, 118.3, 120.2, 125.3, 127.7, 128.1,
130.7, 131.1, 131.8, 132.42, 132.39, 139.3, 142.1, 157.0, 157.8. HRMS
(EI): m/z [M+] calcd for C29H30N2O6S: 534.1825; found: 534.1831.
