$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Library Procedure To a stirred
suspension of the input phenol (3, 1.2 g, 3.71 mmol), polymer-supported
triphenylphosphine (3.7 g, 11.1 mmol) and the alcohol (5.6 mmol) in
dichloromethane (100 mL) was added a solution of
di-tert-butylazodicarboxylate (DTAD) (2.14 g, 9.3 mmol) in
dichloromethane (10 mL) at 0 °C over a period of 1 hour. The resulting
suspension was lightly agitated for 16 hours at room temperature and the
resin was removed by filtration and the filtrate was concentrated to
dryness to afford 7. The resulting residue was dissolved in methanol (20
mL) and divided equally in ten microwave tubes. To each tube was added
bis(triphenylphosphine)palladium chloride (15.1 mg, 0.02 mmol), cesium
fluoride (168 mg, 1.11 mmol) and the boronic acid or ester (0.445 mmol).
The reaction mixtures were heated at 120 °C for 20 minutes, cooled to
room temperature and concentrated to dryness to afford 8. To the
resulting crude reaction mixtures in their microwave tubes was added a
fresh solution methanolic ammonia (7 N, 5 mL) and the reaction mixtures
were heated at 120 °C for 30 minutes. The resulting solutions were cooled
to room temperature, concentrated to dryness and the resulting residues
were dissolved in DMF (1.5 mL) and purified by mass-triggered preparative
LCMS to afford, after evaporation, 9 (12-85%), generally as solids.
Routine 1H-NMR and LCMS data for final compounds can be seen below:
6-(3-Hydroxyphenyl)-3-{[4-(2-morpholin-4-ylpropoxy)phenyl]amino}pyrazine-2-carboxamide
(9a).
6-[3-(Hydroxymethyl)phenyl]-3-({4-[2-(4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)ethoxy]phenyl}amino)-pyrazine-2-carboxamide
(9g). Yield 80%. 1H-NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 2.15 (s, 3H), 2.18-2.44 (m, 8H), 2.68
(t, J= 5.8 Hz, 2H), 4.06 (t, J= 5.8 Hz, 2H), 4.60 (s, 2H), 5.23 (br s,
1H), 6.95 (d, J= 8.9 Hz, 2H), 7.38 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (dd, J1 = 7.6
Hz, J2 = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.60 (d, J= 8.9 Hz, 2H), 8.06 (s, 1H), 8.07 (d, J=
7.6 Hz, 1H), 8.14 (s, 1H), 8.55 (s, 1H), 8.96 (s, 1H), 11.14 (s, 1H) LCMS
(retention time = 1.70 min., purity 100%), ESI+ m/z 463.26 (M+ H)+;
purity determined by 1H-NMR = 100%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (second and third stages), solid-supported reagent
(first stage), thermal (second and third stages), Mitsunobu reaction
(first stage), Suzuki coupling (second stage)
