$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 8. Mitsunobu Reaction: A glass vial,
screwcapped with a teflon-lined septum containing the polymer supported
aminoalcohol (70mg, 0.70 mmol/g) was charged with 2 mL of a stock
solution of tributylphosphine (3.1 mL, 12.6 mmol) and bromophenol (12.6
mmol) in THF (60 mL). The suspension was gently agitated for 10 min and
then cooled to -78°C. 1 mL of a stock solution of TMAD in THF (2.16 g,
12.6 mmol in 31 mL) was then added dropwise with constant agitation. The
reaction mixture was then allowed to slowly warm to room temperature and
agitated for 24 h at ambient temperature and the solution drained. The
beads were washed with 100:1 DMF/TEA (3 x 30 min), 50:50:1 THF/DMF/TEA (3
x 30 min), 100:1 THF/TEA (3 x 30 min), and CH2Cl2 (4 x 30 min); then
dried in vacuo ( house-vacuum for 2h, then high-vacuum for 12 h).
Cleavage of compound from resin was followed by purification and
spectroscopic characterization. 9. Biaryl Coupling: The polymer supported
cyclization precursor (20 mg, 0.60 mmol/g, 0.012mmol) in a glass vial,
screwcapped with a teflon-lined septum was swollen in anhydrous toluene
(2 x 5mL x 20 min) and then dried in vacuo at 50°C for 30 min. The vial
was placed in a bath maintained at 0°C (cryocool) and a pre-cooled
solution of iPrnBu2MgLi1 (4.0 mL of a solution ca. 0.3 M in 2-MeTHF, ca.
100 equiv) was added via syringe and the beads incubated in this solution
at 0°C for 6-8 h. The solution was then removed via cannula under a
positive pressure of Ar, and a pre-cooled solution of CuCN.2LiBr (1.0M in
2-MeTHF, 1.2mL, 100 equiv.) added. The beads were incubated in this
solution at 0°C for 6h and the solution then removed via cannula under a
positive pressure of Ar. A precooled solution of m-dinitrobenzene (1.0M
in 2-MeTHF, 1.2mL, 100 equiv.) was then added and the vials transferred
to a cold cabinet maintained at 6 °C where they were agitated for 12 h.
The beads were then filtered and washed with 8-Hydroxyquinoline (5% w/v
in 50:50:1 THF (stabilized):DMF:TEA; 2 x 10 min, 2 x 12h) with gentle
agitation; then further washed with 50:50:1 THF/DMF/TEA (3 x 30 min),
100:1 THF/TEA (3 x 30 min), and CH2Cl2 (4 x 30 min); then dried in vacuo
( house-vacuum for 2h, then highvacuum for 12 h). Cleavage of compound
from resin was followed by purification and spectroscopic
characterization. (P, 6S,
7R)-7-Methyl-6-phenyl-8-(3-phenyl-propyl)-6,7,8,9-tetrahydro-5-oxa-1,8-diaza-dibenzo[a,c]cyclononen-11-ol,
c-A1B4C4D2, 7. Colorless oil. Yield: 80%. Rf = 0.30 (Triethylamine washed
SiO2, Hexanes/EtOAc/Et3N: 25:75:1). Rf = 0.30 δH (500MHz, C6D6): 0.98 (d,
J7Hz, 3H, CHCH3), 1.67 (app. quintet, J7Hz, 2H, C(15)H2), 2.39 (app.
quintet, J7Hz, 1H, C(14)HH'), 2.47 (app. quintet, J6.5Hz, 1H, C(14)HH'),
2.53 (app. quintet, J6.5Hz, 1H, C(16)HH'), 2.62 (app. quintet, J6.5Hz,
1H, C(16)HH'), 2.96 (q, J7Hz, 1H, C(7)H), 3.32 (d, J14Hz, 1H, C(9)HH'),
3.48 (d, J14Hz, 1H, C(9)HH'), 4.98 (s, 1H, C(6)H), 6.52 (dd, J8Hz, 4.5Hz,
1H, C(3)H), 6.70 (dd, J8Hz, 1Hz, 1H, C(4)H), 6.82 (dd, J8.5Hz, 2Hz, 1H,
C(12)H), 7.08 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.12-7.19 (m, 8H, Ar-H), 7.30 (d, J2Hz, 1H,
C(10)H), 7.66 (d, J8.5Hz, 1H, C(13)H), 8.31 (dd, J4.5Hz, 1Hz, 1H, C(2)H).
δc (125MHz, C6D6): 14.7 (-CHCH3), 30.5 (C-15), 33.6 (C-16), 55.3 (C-9),
57.6 (C-14), 67.5 (C-7), 85.2 (C-1), 115.4 (C-12), 117.5 (C-10), 123.3
(C-3), 125.8, 126.1, 126.5 (C- 4), 127.2, 127.9, 128.1, 128.3, 128.5,
128.9, 131,3 (C-13), 141.2 (quat.), 142.6 (quat.), 144.1 (C-2), 153.9
(quat.), 154.0 (quat.), 158.0 (quat.). m/z (ESI): 451 (MH+100%). HRMS
found 451.2390. C30H31N2O2 (MH+) requires 451.2385.
