$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the Mitsunobu Reaction Using DPPBE Synthesis of
4-Phenethyloxy-benzoic Acid Methyl Ester (Table 1, entry 2): To a
solution of 2-phenylethanol (1 mmol) in THF (3 mL) was added successively
methyl 4-hydroxy-benzoate (1.2 mmol) and DPPBE (1.3 mmol, 0.5 M/THF). A
solution of DIAD (1.3 mmol) in THF (0.5 mL) was added drop wise over 15
min at r.t. and the progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC.
Typically after 1 h tetrabutyl-ammonium fluoride in THF (1 M, 2.5 mmol)
was added. After 1 h at r.t. the reaction was concentrated to dryness and
the residue was taken-up in EtOAc, washed with aq NaOH, H2O and brine,
dried (MgSO4), filtered and evaporated to dryness. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography using hexane-EtOAc (95:5) to give
4-phenethyloxy-benzoic acid methyl ester. Clear oil, yield 79%. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 3.06 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 3.81 (s, 3 H), 4.28
(t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.06 (d, J = 9 Hz, 2 H), 7.34- 7.21 (m, 5 H), 7.90
(d, J = 9 Hz, 2 H). MS (ES): m/z = 257 [MH]+. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 165.8, 162.2, 138.0, 131.2, 128.9, 128.3, 126.3, 121.8, 114.4, 68.4,
51.7, 34.7. HRMS (FAB) calcd for C16H16O3 [M - H+]+: 256.109945. Found:
256.109963.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction, optimization study of phosphine reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Removable phosphine reagents for the Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yoakim, Christiane; Guse, I.; O'Meara, J. A.; Thavonekham, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (4), 473-476

