$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A 25 mL round bottom flask was charged with monophenol (1.04 g, 2.80
mmol, 1 equiv), homoallylic alcohol (914 mg, 3.09 mmol, 1.1 equiv), and
PPh3 (810 mg, 3.09 mmol, 1.1 equiv). The contents of the flask was
dissolved with 8 mL of dichloromethane and cooled to 0 °C. Diisopropyl
azodicarboxylate (DIAD) (606 μL, 3.09 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added dropwise
and the bath was allowed to expire. The reaction was stirred for a total
of 26 h in the dark at room temperature and then concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was loaded directly onto a silica column and purified (40%
EtOAc/petroleum ether). Product, yield 1.42 g, 79%. Yellow foam. [α]25D =
+73.1 (c 0.4, CHCl3); IR (neat/NaCl) 1766, 1600; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.56 (d, J = 8.5, 2 H), 7.35-7.32 (m, 3 H), 7.18 (d, J = 8.5, 2 H),
7.15 (d, J = 8.5, 2 H), 6.94 (d, J = 16.5, 1 H), 6.34 (d, J = 1.5, 1 H),
6.14 (d, J = 1.5, 1 H), 5.63 (dddd, J = 7, 7, 14, 17.5, 1 H), 5.16 (t, J
= 6, 1 H), 4.96-4.93 (m, 2 H), 3.74 (s, 3 H), 2.59 (ddd, J = 6.5, 6.5,
14, 1 H), 2.45 (ddd, J = 6.5, 6.5, 14, 1 H), 2.32 (s, 3 H), 2.26 (s, 3
H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 194.0, 169.1, 168.9, 158.0, 155.6, 152.6,
152.3, 148.8, 144.3, 140.8, 132.5, 132.3, 129.6, 128.6, 127.9, 122.2,
121.5, 118.7, 116.6, 100.3, 98.6, 79.3, 76.7, 56, 42.3, 21.2, 21.1; HRMS
(ELS) m/z calcd for C31H27F3NaO10S [M + Na]+ 671.1175, found 671.1174.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Structural Reassignment of (+)-Epicalyxin F
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tian, Xia; Rychnovsky, Scott D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(24), 4955-4958

