$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedures:
3-Isopropyloxyphenyl Benzoate. An oven dried flask was purged with
nitrogen and immersed in a water bath containing ice. It was then charged
with resorcinol monobenzoate (6.0 g, 28 mmol), PPh3 (9.6 g, 36.4 mmol),
propan-2-ol (1.7 g, 28 mmol), and dry THF (50 mL). Diisopropyl
azodicarboxylate (6.3 g, 30.8 mmol) was then added dropwise over 15 min.
The solution was kept at 0 °C for a further 15 min and allowed to warm to
r.t. and stirred during 4 h, after which the solution was concentrated
under reduced pressure and the residue was triturated with a mixture of
Et2O and hexane to give a pink solid. The suspension was filtered and the
filtrate was concentrated to give a brown oil which was placed on a
column of silica gel and eluted with EtOAc:hexane (0.5:9.5) afforded
compound. 3-Alkoxyphenyl Benzoate Derivative, Yield: 76%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
