$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of S-or R-Methyl 2-(4-bromo-phenoxy)-3-phenyl-propanoate
(5d). A solution of diisopropylazodicarboxylate (DIAD, 2.81 g, 13.90
mmol) in anhydrous toluene (20 mL) was added dropwise to an ice-bath
cooled mixture of R-or S-methyl phenyllactate (2.51 g, 13.87 mmol),
4-bromophenol (2.45 g, 13.89 mmol) and triphenylphosphine (3.64 g, 13.88
mmol) in anhydrous toluene (50 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature overnight, under N2 atmosphere. Toluene was evaporated
in vacuo and a mixture of Et2O and hexane (50 mL, 1:1) was added to the
residue. The resulting precipitate was filtered off and the filtrate was
evaporated to dryness. The residue was chromatographed on a silica gel
column (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate 9:1 as eluent) affording the
desired compound as a colorless oil in 76% yields. S-Methyl
2-(4-bromo-phenoxy)-3-phenyl-propanoate (5d): colorless oil in 76% yield.
GC/MS, m/z (%): 336 (61) [M++2], 334 (61) [M+], 196 (25), 163 (72), 121
(100); 1H NMR: δ 3.23 (dd, 2H, CH2), 3.71 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.76 (t, 1H, CH),
6.68-6.86, 7.01-7.19 and 7.21-7.42 (m, 9H, aromatics).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis, characterization and biological evaluation of
vreidofibrate-like derivatives endowed with peroxisome
proliferator-activated receptor activity
