$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To further confirm this structural assignment we treated, as previously,
a solution of N-Boc neomycin B 4 (1 equiv) and triphenyl phosphine (10
equiv) in THF with DIAD (10 equiv). The reaction product was isolated and
acetylated to provide the pentaacetate 9 in 75% yield (two steps) (Scheme
2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroxyl Substitution Studies at the 5''-Position in the Neomycin B
