$DATUM Synthesis of thioether-substituted thiacalix[4]monocrowns 3,4 Thioethers
2 (0.25 mmol) and TPP (0.52 g, 2 mmol) were dissolved in toluene (10 mL)
and oligoethylene glycols were added (1 mmol). After that, DEAD (0.31 mL.
2 mmol) was added dropwise. After 3 h, toluene was removed under reduced
pressure, residue was suspended in methanol (50 mL) and precipitate was
filtered. Compound 3a: white powder. Mp 290-293 °C, R f (Hex:EtOAc = 4:1)
= 0.67. anal. calcd. for C52H70O6S6: C 63.50, H 7.17; found: C 63.37, H
8.29. m/z (p-NA) 1007.3 [M+Na]+, 1023.3 [M+K]+. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz,
303K) 7.41 (s, 4H, Harom), 7.33 (s, 4H, Harom), 3.99 (m, 8H,
ArOCH2+ArOCH2CH2O), 3.50 (t, 3 J HH = 3.8 Hz, 4H, ArOCH2CH2O), 2.49 (s,
4H, OCH2), 2.05 (s, 6H, CH3), 1.93 (t, 3 J HH = 8.5 Hz, 4H, CH2S), 1.32
(s, 36H, t-Bu).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction
