$DATUM (S)-tert-Butyl
2-iodo-4-methoxy-3-(1-(trimethylsilyl)oct-7-en-1-yn-3-yloxy)benzyl
(methyl)carbamate (14). To a solution of phenol 3 (774 mg, 1.97 mmol) in
THF (18 mL) was added PPh3 (938 mg, 3.58 mmol) and a solution of the
propargylic alcohol 13 (351 mg, 1.79 mmol) in THF (4 mL). This solution
was stirred for 5 min before the dropwise addition of DIAD (0.70 mL, 3.58
mmol). The reaction was then heated to reflux and stirred for 3.5 h. The
reaction mixture was cooled and concentrated in vacuo giving a brown
orange oil. Purification by flash column chromatography on silica gel
(5.0 cm x 8 cm) eluting with EtOAc/hexane (1:19-1:10) afforded the
desired ether 14, yield 835 mg, 1.46 mmol, 74% as a colourless oil. [α]D
= +11.5 (c 0.5, CHCl3, 27 °C); FT-IR (neat) νmax 2957 (w), 2934 (w), 2865
(w), 2838 (w), 2175 (w), 1696 (s), 1640 (w), 1589 (w), 1476 (m), 1389 (m)
cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.87 (1H, br d, J =6.7 Hz, C5ArH), 6.81
(1H, m, C6ArH), 5.87 (1H, ddt, J =17.1, 10.3, 6.7 Hz, H2C=CH-), 5.20 (1H,
m, ArOCH), 5.07 (1H, dq, J = 17.1, 1.8 Hz), 4.99 (1H, ddt, J =10.3, 1.8,
1.3 Hz), 4.46 (2H, br, -NCH2-), 3.84 (3H, s, OCH3), 2.83 (3H, br, -NCH3),
2.18 (2H, br q, J = 6.7 Hz, H2C=CHCH2-), 2.10-1.93 (2H, m, OCHCH2-),
1.86-1.65 (2H, m, OCHCH2CH2-), 1.51 and 1.44 (9H, br, -OC(CH3)3), 0.04
(9H, s, -Si(CH3)3) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3, C2Ar not observed) δ
156.34 (C, -C=O), 151.83 (C, C4Ar), 146.63 (C, C3Ar), 138.98 (CH,
H2C=CH-), 132.71 (C, C1Ar), 123.52 and 122.49 (CH, C6Ar), 115.00 (CH2,
H2C=CH-), 112.46 (CH, C5Ar), 104.07 (C, -CCTMS), 92.60 (C, -CCTMS), 80.06
(C, -C(CH3)3), 72.21 (CH, ArOCH-), 57.99 and 56.92 (CH2, -NCH2-), 56.36
(CH3, OCH3), 35.67 (CH2, OCHCH2), 34.44 (CH3, -NCH3), 28.79 (CH3,
-C(CH3)3), 24.90 (CH2, H2C=CHCH2CH2-), 0.06 (CH3, -Si(CH3)3) ppm; LRMS
(ES+) m/z 572 [M+H+], 594 [M+Na+]; HRMS (ES+) for C25H38INNaO4Si,
calculated 594.1507, found 594.1504 Da.
