$DATUM 3-((S)-1-Cyclopropyl-but-3-enyloxy)-4,5-dimethoxy-benzoic acid methyl
ester (S)-4 Under N2, the benzoic methyl ester 5 (1 g, 4.71 mmol, 1
equiv) was dissolved in THF (13 mL). The homoallylic alcohol (R)-6 (0.528
g, 4.71 mmol, 1 equiv), PPh3 (1.234 g, 4.71 mmol, 1 equiv) and NEt3 (0.1
mL, 0.707 mmol, 0.15 equiv) were added. The mixture was cooled to 0°C,
then DIAD (0.931 mL, 4.71 mmol, 1 equiv) in 2 mL THF was added dropwise.
The reaction mixture was allowed to stir at rt for 2 h, then it was
checked by LCMS and TLC; the same amounts of homoallylic alcohol, PPh3,
and DIAD were added to complete the reaction. TLC (AcOEt/cHex 1:9, Rf
0.21, stained with vanillin). The reaction mixture was evaporated to
dryness, then purified by FC (AcOEt/cHex 1:9) to give a colorless oil.
Yield: 1.05 g, 73 %. 3-((S)-1-Cyclopropyl-but-3-enyloxy)-4,
5-dimethoxy-benzoic acid methyl ester (S)-4, yield 1.05 g, 73 % 1H-NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.25 (d, J= 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.22 (d, J= 1.6 Hz,1H),
5.86-5.96 (m, 1H), 5.00-5.1 (m, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.82 (s,
3H), 3.67-3.72 (m, 1H), 2.49-2.51 (t, J= 6.25 Hz, 2H), 1.03-1.12 (m, 1H),
0.40-0.50 (m, 2H), 0.15-0.28 (m, 2H). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 166.6,
153.2, 151.6, 144.1, 134.2, 124.8, 117.2, 112.2, 106.8, 83.6, 60.8, 56.1,
52.1, 39.4, 14.9, 3.6, 2.1. LCMS ESI+ (method A) not ionizing. Retention
time (Rt): 2.70 min. UV: 233, 265 nm. Chiral HPLC: Method 1, 72 % ee.
HRMS : [M+Na]+ calculated for C17H22O5 329.1359, observed 329.1352.
