$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thioethers 2a-c 1.00 g (1.4 mmol)
thiacalix[4]arene 1 and 1.46 g (5.6 mmol) TPP were dissolved in THF (30
mL) and appropriate thioalkyl alcohol (13.9 mmol) was added. After that,
0.87mL (5.6 mmol) DEAD was added dropwise at -10 °C and stirred at r.t.
for 1 day; and then, heated to 40-50 °C and stirred for 16 h. After
completion of reaction, THF was removed under reduced pressure and
methanol was added to residue, precipitate was filtered and dried in
vacuum. Compound 2b: white powder. Mp 137-139 °C(decomp.). R f (diethyl
ether:petroleum ether = 1:8) = 0.41. anal. calcd. for C58H68O4S6 *2C5H12
*Et2O: C 69.74, H 8.29; found: C 69.75, H 8.52. Maldi TOF (Ultraflex
Bruker) m/z (p-NA) 1044.3 [M+Na]+, 1060.3 [M+K]+. 1H NMR (CDCl3 , 400
MHz, 303K) 7.81 (s, 2H, OH), 7.67 (s, 4H, Harom), 7.37-7.29 (m, 10H, Ph),
6.94 (s, 4H, Harom), 4.59 (t, 3 J HH = 7.0 Hz, 4H, OCH2), 3.84 (s, 4H,
SCH2Ph), 3.03 (t, 3 J HH = 7.1 Hz, 4H, CH2SBz), 1.35 (s, 18H, t-Bu), 0.79
(s, 18H, t-Bu).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative solvent toluene gave lower yield, Mitsunobu reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of Thiacalix[4]monocrowns Modified by
Thioether Groups on the Lower Rim
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
