$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Cyclization of
4-Hydroxy-3-(hydroxyalkyl)-1-methyl-2(1H)quinolinones To a stirred
solution of 2.79 mmol of the 4-hydroxy-3-(hydroxyalkyl) quinolinone and
2.79 mmol of triphenylphosphine in 50 mL of tetrahydrofuran was added
drop-wise a solution of 2.79 mmol of diethyl azodicarboxylate in 5 mL of
tetrahydrofuran. The mixture ,was stirred at room temperature for 1-2 hr,
then the solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was
flash chromatographed using CH2Cl2/MeOH (99:1) to elute the products.
6-Methyl-2,3,4,6-tetrahydropyrano[3,2-c]quinolin-5-one (8), yield 73%.
m.p. 108°C-110°C. IR (CH2Cl2): 1622, 1597 cm-1; 1H-NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.91
(dd, J= 8.09 and 1.47 Hz, 1H), 7.56-7.50 (m, 1H), 7.32 (d, J= 8.46Hz,
1H), 7.22 (t, 1H), 4.33 (t, 2H), 3.70 (s, 3H), 2.65 (t, 2H), 2.10-2.03
(m, 2H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3): δ 163.24, 156.54, 138.39, 130.03, 122.51,
121.42, 116.15, 113.71, 106.93, 66.94, 29.19, 21.46, 19.66. MS: m/z 216
(MH+). Anal. Calc. for C13H13NO2: C, 72.54; H, 6.09; N, 6.51. Found: C,
72.48; H, 6.14; N, 6.49.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu condition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cyclization of 4-hydroxy-3-hydroxyalkylcarbostyrils under Mitsunobu
conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Coppola, Gary M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2004), 34(18), 3381-3387

