$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Mitsunobu reaction:
1-Nitro-4-(3-phenylpropoxy)benzene: The general procedure above was
followed, using 3-phenyl-1-propanol (16.4 mg, 0.120 mmol), 4-nitrophenol
(18.1 mg, 0.130 mmol), oligomer 2 (88 mg, 0.246 mmol), and oligomer 4
(2.1 mmol/g, 116.5 mg, 0.245 mmol) in 0.6 mL THF. Filtration through a
plug of silica with 4:1 heptane/EtOAc afforded (22.5 mg, 73%) of an
inseparable mixure of 1-Nitro-4-(3-phenylpropoxy)benzene and
3-phenylpropyl ether (85:15) as an off-white solid. TLC (4:1
Heptane/EtOAc) Rf 0.45; IR (thin film) 3109, 3085, 2939, 1606, 1593,
1514, 1497, 1340, 1269, 1109, 845, 754 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
1-Nitro-4-(3-phenylpropoxy)benzene: 8.19 (d, 2H, J = 9.3 Hz), 7.33-7.28
(m, 2H), 7.23-7.18 (m, 3H), 6.93 (d, 2H, J = 9.3 Hz), 4.05 (t, 2H, J =
6.3 Hz), 2.83 (t, 2H, J = 7.4 Hz), 2.17 (dt, 2H, J = 7.4, 6.3 Hz);
3-phenylpropyl ether: 7.33-7.28 (m, 0.7H), 7.23-7.18 (m, 1.1H), 3.40 (t,
0.71H, J = 6.6 Hz), 2.78 (t, 0.76H, J = 7.2 Hz), 2.17 (dt, 0.71H, J =
7.2, 6.6 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) 164.1, 141.4, 140.9, 140.5, 128.5,
128.5, 128.5, 128.4, 126.1, 125.9, 67.7, 34.1, 34.0, 33.1, 31.9, 30.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Mitsunobu reaction, oligomeric triphenylphophine used, polymeric
azodicarboxylate used
